# How to cite this software. GitHub shows a "Cite this repository" button from
# this file, and Zenodo uses it when archiving each release.
# Update version and date-released with each release.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Orbit Coordinate Converter"
abstract: >-
  Converts ECEF X/Y/Z coordinates and CCSDS OEM orbit files to WGS84
  latitude, longitude, and altitude, rotating space-fixed frames (EME2000,
  GCRF, ICRF, TEME) to Earth-fixed. Handles files with millions of points and
  exports trajectories in the format used by NASA's NAIRAS radiation model.
authors:
  - given-names: Samuel
    family-names: Braman
version: 1.5.0
date-released: 2026-11-05
license: MIT
# Zenodo concept DOI: always resolves to the latest release
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23986346"
repository-code: "https://github.com/SBK008/orbit-coordinate-converter"
url: "https://github.com/SBK008/orbit-coordinate-converter"
keywords:
  - ECEF
  - WGS84
  - CCSDS
  - OEM
  - orbit
  - coordinate conversion
  - NAIRAS
